+## Block 4: Weather service
+
+Gets the forecast for a city and dates from Open-Meteo (free, no key) and says what
+each day needs from an outfit: warmth, types and materials to prefer or avoid,
+waterproof, evening layer. It never picks clothes itself.
+
+```bash
+cd wardrobe-ai/services/weather
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+python -m uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8004
+```
+
+Open **http://127.0.0.1:8004/docs**. With the wardrobe service also running,
+`python outfit_demo.py Goa --user u1` picks an outfit per day from that user's
+clothes. Details: [`services/weather/README.md`](services/weather/README.md) and
+[`services/weather/GUIDE.md`](services/weather/GUIDE.md).
